Yes, 3 Kirk Brae is in the Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Under the council's windows guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material or the style (for example, swapping timber for uPVC, or changing the glazing pattern), you will likely need to apply. If the replacements exactly match the originals, you may not need one.

Because I can't give a formal opinion on your specific proposal, I'd suggest either contacting the planning desk with your plans or submitting a pre-application enquiry before you order the windows. If you already have an application reference for this property, I can look up its status for you.
